From 1b73a5e9dae0d6f0ebb494bb1df94965776c8a01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ozgur Guzeldereli <ozgur@guzeldereli.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:40:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] TTF Q38 prefill: TQ1_P expert MUL_MAT_ID via Q4_0 MMQ;
 per-expert side vectors stay off the -ncmoe CPU override

- batched TQ1_P MUL_MAT_ID: expand the trits to Q4_0 (d = 1, nibble = v + 8, exact) in a pool buffer and run the
  Q4_0 MMQ kernels instead of the per-expert fallback (host sync, dequantise + cuBLAS per expert); mmq.cu tolerates
  a src0 with no buffer (the pool copy)
- LLM_FFN_EXPS_REGEX skips .ttf_c/.ttf_m/.ttf_r/.ttf_b: on the CPU their GET_ROWS and the elementwise ops on
  [n_ff, n_tokens*top_k] ran there and split the graph 167 times per ubatch

Q38 r4s1000 (40.4 GB), 3090 Ti, -ncmoe 33 -lm none, pp2048 at ub 2048: 213 -> 787 tok/s; pp4096 at ub 4096 955.
---
